{
  "$comment": "The studio palette (#241). One row per element an author can place, each naming the bpmn-support.json row it claims to offer. Membership is NOT this file's to decide: createManifestPaletteProvider offers only rows whose manifest entry is studio=supported, so withdrawing an element in the manifest removes it from the palette with no edit here. This file carries presentation -- label, icon, group -- which the manifest has no business holding. BpmnPaletteManifestTests fails if a row names a manifest entry that does not exist, if a supported element has no row and no stated reason, or if the groups drift from the order below. Entries whose manifest row is not `supported` stay listed on purpose: their className is what createManifestMenuFilter uses to strip them from bpmn-js's own Create-element popup and replace menu, which are separate surfaces the palette override does not reach (#264).",
  "$fields": {
    "id": "bpmn-js palette entry id. 'create.*' places a shape; 'append.*' attaches to the selection.",
    "label": "What the author reads in the palette.",
    "description": "One-line hint, shown as the entry's title.",
    "group": "Palette section; must appear in groupOrder.",
    "className": "bpmn-js icon class.",
    "type": "The bpmn moddle type the element factory creates.",
    "createFactory": "Set instead of `type` for entries bpmn-js builds through a dedicated factory (participants).",
    "eventDefinitionType": "Event definition to attach, where the type alone does not identify the element.",
    "properties": "Extra businessObject properties set at creation (isExpanded, triggeredByEvent, isForCompensation).",
    "localName": "The bpmn-support.json row's localName. The join key -- a typo here fails the drift test.",
    "eventDefinition": "The bpmn-support.json row's eventDefinition. Null where the row has none.",
    "menuClassNames": "Additional bpmn-js icon classes for the SAME element, used only by the menu filter (#264). bpmn-js names some elements differently in its own popups than the palette does -- 'bpmn-icon-business-rule' vs the palette's 'bpmn-icon-business-rule-task'. A deny key that matches nothing silently leaves the element reachable, so BpmnPaletteManifestTests asserts every key here and every withheld className actually appears in the vendored bundle."
  },
  "groupOrder": [
    "Events",
    "Tasks",
    "Gateways",
    "Containers",
    "Collaboration",
    "Artifacts",
    "Boundary Events"
  ],
  "notOnThePalette": [
    {
      "localName": "sequenceFlow",
